> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @ground beef{3/10%lb}, @dry jasmine rice{3/10%cup}, @baby bok choy{2/5} (chopped), @garlic cloves{4/5} (minced), @ginger{1/5%tbsp} (grated), @sesame oil{1/5%tbsp}, @green onions{2/5} (sliced), @cilantro{1/20%cup}, @coconut milk{1/5%can} (can size 13.5 oz), @gluten-free chicken or beef broth{3/5%cup}, @gluten-free gochujang{2/5%tbsp}, @gluten-free tamari{1/5%tbsp}, @lime juice{1/5%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{2/5%tsp}, @?gluten-free chili crisp per serving{1/5%tsp}.

== Preparation ==

Cook the jasmine rice separately. Brown the beef and set it aside to keep its texture. Cook garlic and ginger in sesame oil, add coconut milk, broth, gochujang and tamari, then simmer with bok choy. Finish with lime and vinegar; serve over rice with beef, herbs and optional chili crisp.
